{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And you shall serve YHWH your Elohim</b> — speaks in plural language, for the prayer of the many is not rejected. And it says, 'and He will bless your bread' — singular language, for each and every one is blessed according to his own situation." "<b>וברך</b> — Three times in the Masorah. And the others: וברך פרי בטנך, and וברך עלי את אלקנה ואת אשתו. As stated in Berakhot, regarding the cup of blessing: one sends it to the people of his household so that the fruit of her womb be blessed — and this is וברך את לחמך ואת מימיך, that he blessed the blessing after the meal and sent it to his wife and blessed the fruit of her womb. And likewise Boaz, who blessed Elkanah and his wife, and she conceived — and this is וברך עלי וברך פרי בטנך." "<b>מימיך</b> — Three times of this form. And the others: ואם מימיך נשתה וגו', and מחוטב עציך עד שואב מימיך. ואם מימיך נשתה and ונתתי מכרם — to say that even though he blessed their waters and they did not need other waters, they still purchased from them. As they said: from here, an innkeeper who has his own supplies — it is the way of the world that he should purchase from the host in order to benefit him." "<b>והסירותי</b> — Two times in the Masorah. Here, and the other: והסידותי את כפי. Because Moses received the countenance of the Shekhinah, he merited והסירותי מחלה, for it is written of him: לא כהתה עינו ולא נס לחה." "<b>והסירותי מחלה מקרבך</b> — and adjacent to it: לא תהיה משכלה. Since the illness departed, there shall be no miscarriage. וגם את מספר ימיך אמלא — אמלא עולה 72 — ימי שנותינו בהם שבעים שנה, excluding the year in which he was born and the year in which he died."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {1 "The citation 'וברך עלי את אלקנה ואת אשתו' does not correspond to any known biblical verse; the reference to Boaz alongside Elkanah is likewise unclear, possibly a conflation of traditions.", 3 "The masorah note pairs והסירותי (with resh) and והסידותי (with dalet), the latter occurring in Exodus 33:17; the link to Moses' merit is based on the juxtaposition."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:20.875258384Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}